      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Generally would like to see this as a base feature of VRC as part of the scene descriptor. Right alongside \"RunSpeed\" might be \"FlightSpeed\" -- set flight speed to 0 to disable. Otherwise, double jump to enable. Old, un-updated worlds where this variable isn't present could be presumed to have a certain \"default\" flight speed.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-12-24T08:40:35.718Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A really cool thing to see in worlds is an option to fly, WITHOUT having to add colliders to your model to do so.\nWhat I want is for world creators to have a new player mod option to enable flight. Could be enabled just by jumping while mid-air maybe? (So double jump.) (By having it an option to enable on worlds will prevent it from being used on worlds that don't want it permitted.)\n\nAnother small thing to help it not look so 'meh' is to have a flight animation option on avatars, with a default flight animation for models that don't have custom animations.\n(See my other post for more detail on my custom animations requests. https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/more-custom-animation-options)",
